https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_NzLs-xSss0  (Capo 2) (MC2)

TIP:  There’s a (G) (F) - (C) hook that permeates the song.  In the verse the (F) occurs on the last word of the phrase followed by a quick movement to (C).

TIP:  The (G) (Gadd) transition can be skipped in favor of holding the (G) if you want.  If transposing, play the transposed root and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  For (Cadd9) you’ll be playing a (C) so just add your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret.

TIP:  For (C) - (C/F) - (CaddG) sequence, hold the (C) shape, then roll your index finger down on the 1st fret to cover note <f> on the 1st string/1st fret.  Still holding the (C/F), add your pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret to get to (CaddG).  Really quite easy.    

TIP:  In the second instrumental you stick with (D), or you can play (D/A) by adding your pinky to cover the <f#> at the the 4th string/4th fret.  Sounds a little better.

TIP:  For the long electric piano bit, play (Gsus4) - you have to play something to keep pace before the drums come in so it might as well be this.  Form up a standard (G), then remove your fingers from strings 5 and 6 so all you’ve got is your pinky on the 1st string/3rd fret note <g>.  Now strum strings 1-3 while adding and removing your index finger to note <c> at the 2nd string/1st fret, on-off, on-off, 1-2-3-4, 1-2-3-4 . . . through Keith’s drums signaling the end of the sequence. 


